-- title:
--   Centred closed special points lie on an Igusa branch (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the corresponding $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field.
--
--   **Data.** A prime $q$ with $q = 2$ (`hq2`); a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by the $j$-expansion `jqModC` and its $M'$-expansion `jqNModC`) which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places, namely the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j_{\mathrm{geom}}) \in$ `ssJSet q` (the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves have trivial $q$-torsion over the given field); the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into `fieldBar q M'`; a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (an element of `Idx q`); and two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'`: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $= \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   **The constant reduction $R_0$.** $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, subject to: the preimage of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ under the constants is $A$; $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ is compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants; every nonzero element can be rescaled by a constant into $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue; $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ preserves degrees; and the push-forward of principal divisors is compatible with orders of residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The Igusa family.** `hIg_inf`: $f$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, where $\infty =$ `lineInfty q` $= [1:0]$, if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ after coefficientwise inclusion into $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$. `hIg`: for every line $\ell$ there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries $\infty$ to $\ell$ and with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` (the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` attached to $\zeta$ and $\gamma$ by `IsLevelAutBar`, the identity if no such automorphism exists). `hIg_inj`: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective. `hIg_perm`: for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with $(O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell))$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma\ell)$ for all $\ell$.
--
--   **The supersingular family.** `hSS_A`: for each $s \in W$ and $x \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ if and only if $x \in A$. `hSS_over`: for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the element given by the coefficientwise image of $j_q$ has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and (the image of) $a$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix`: each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: for each $s$ there is $t \in O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that for every $a \in A$ the difference $t - a$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   **The regular prolongation.** $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring with a surjective residue map onto that field, with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, with the preimage of the constants equal to $A$, and with every nonzero element rescalable into the integers with nonzero residue), and `hR` identifies $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$. `hR₀O`: an element $f$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic hypotheses.** An element $\pi \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$ (`hπ`, `hπP`). A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, such that the valuation ring $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0 \cap A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`: $x \in A_1$ iff $x \in A$), assumed to be a Henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   **Quantified data of the conclusion.** `fieldBar q M'` is given the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained from the constants. For every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` satisfying: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all the constants is everything; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition — for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in $E(K') := k_0(\,\text{image of }K'\,) \sqcup F_0$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ then all $a_i = 0$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $E_1 := E(K_1)$. For every $A_1$-algebra structure on $E_1$ whose structure map sends $a \in A_1$ to the image of $a$ in `fieldBar q M'`, and every $j_1 \in E_1$ with $j_1 \neq 0$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the element given by the coefficientwise image of $j_q$, consider the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ E₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the middle chart into `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $E_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and `chartAlgInf` (those integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), with structure morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` from $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \mathrm{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin`, $X_{\infty} = \mathrm{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf`, and `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$.
--
--   Three predicates are introduced. `InStalk x f`, for $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in E_1$: for every $y \in X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with `ιFin` mapping $y$ to $x$ there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f\,h = g$ in $E_1$, and likewise for every $y \in X_{\infty}$ above $x$ with $g,h$ in `chartAlgInf`. `InMax x f`: the same, with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in each chart. `Centred P x`, for a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$: $P$ is rational (the constants surject onto its residue field) and for every $f \in E_1$ with `InStalk x f` one has $f \in P.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. A fourth predicate `GoodPt x` is also introduced — `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; in each of the two charts, every $b$ whose image lies in the non-units of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in every prime above $x$; and for every $y \in X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ above $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ avoids `ssJSet q Ω` — but the conclusion does not refer to `GoodPt`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ such that `Centred P x` holds, `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$, and $x$ specialises only to itself, there exists a line $\ell_b \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ such that:
--
--   (1) for every $y \in X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ mapped to $x$ by `ιFin` and every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin`, if the image of $b$ in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_b)$ then $b \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$;
--
--   (2) for every $y \in X_{\infty}$ mapped to $x$ by `ιInf` and every $b \in$ `chartAlgInf`, if the image of $b$ is a non-unit of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_b)$ then $b \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$;
--
--   (3) every $b \in$ `chartAlgInf` has image in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_b)$;
--
--   (4) every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` has image in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell_b)$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the assertion that a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model, at which a $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-rational place of the full level-$(q^2M', H)$ field is centred, lies on one of the Igusa branches indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$: both chart algebras are contained in the corresponding Igusa valuation ring, and the non-units of that ring are carried into the primes above the point. It feeds the two results that move such a centred point by a level automorphism, used in the construction of the semistable covering of the model.
